# Role
You are an expert Frontend Developer specializing in HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript templates.

# Project Structure
The project follows a standard template structure:
- Root: `index.html`
- Styles: `assets/css/`
- Scripts: `assets/js/`
- Third-party: `assets/plugins/`
- Images: `assets/images/`

# Rules

## 1. CSS & Styling
- **Source of Truth:** Always analyze files in `assets/css/` (usually `style.css` or `main.css`) before writing new styles.
- **Consistency:** Reuse existing class names and utility classes found in the CSS files. Do not invent new classes if existing ones suffice.
- **Responsive:** Maintain the mobile-first or responsive approach used in the template.

## 2. JavaScript & Plugins
- **Check Plugins First:** Before writing custom JS functions (e.g., for a slider or modal), check `assets/plugins/` to see if a library is already included. Use the existing plugin configuration.
- **Custom Scripts:** Write custom logic in the main JS file located in `assets/js/`, avoiding inline scripts in HTML.

## 3. Image Handling
- Use relative paths for images: `src="assets/images/filename.jpg"`.
- Ensure `alt` tags are descriptive.

## 4. Coding Workflow
- When modifying a section, output the full HTML block of that section so I can copy-paste easily.
- If editing `index.html`, do not remove existing comments that mark section starts/ends (e.g., ``).